  "misconceptions": [
    "The student believes the denominator indicates the number of gaps needed to mark a fraction rather than the total number of equal parts.",
    "The student confuses the position of a fraction with the number of intervals required to reach it (e.g., thinking 1/3 requires 2 gaps because it is the second mark)."
  ],
  "prerequisite": "Understanding that the denominator represents the total number of equal parts into which the whole is divided."
